  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—namely, the favorable outcome probabilities (33% vs. 34%) and their difference—is explicitly mentioned in the verbal report. The individual recognizes that Lottery B has a higher probability of a favorable outcome and highlights this as a relevant factor. The justification centers on this probability difference, even though the individual concludes the lotteries are roughly equal. The decision reason’s rule—preferring the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome—is directly aligned with the individual’s stated consideration. Although the individual does not explicitly state 'I chose B because it has a higher probability of winning,' the fact that they focus on the 1 percentage point advantage of B and mention it as a key differentiating factor strongly indicates that this criterion influenced their judgment. The spontaneity of the decision does not negate the influence of this reason, as the verbal report still reveals it as a considered factor. Therefore, the decision reason was used, albeit with a minor qualification due to the individual's perception of near-equality.",
  "final_assessment_score": 85
